## Create Your Azure AI Foundry Project (New)
# Go to Azure AI Foundry > Click “Create New Project” > Choose "Microsoft Foundry Resource" >
# Give it a name > Select Azure subscription, RG, region > Create

## Set Up Your Master Agent
# In your project, click “Agents” in the left sidebar > New Agent
# Click “Create Agent”
# Name your agent: “MasterAgent”
# Select your model GPT-4.1 for better reasoning

## Writing the Master Agent System Prompt
You are a routing agent.

Decide which agent should handle the request:

- DataAgent → for calculations, data processing
- ResponseAgent → for explanations or answers

Return ONLY one word:
DataAgent
or
ResponseAgent

Do not include context, explanation, or formatting.

# Paste this prompt into the “Instructions” field > Save.

## Create Your Worker Agents
# Click “Create Agent” again > Name: “DataAgent”
# System prompt:
You are a Data Retrieval Agent.

ORIGINAL REQUEST:
{{input}}

ROUTING DECISION:
{{LatestMessage}}

Your job is to:
1. Analyze the ORIGINAL REQUEST
2. Perform calculations or data processing
3. Return only the result

IMPORTANT:
- Always use the ORIGINAL REQUEST above
- No explanations or extra text
Format: Start with "DATA FINDINGS:" then provide results

# # Paste this prompt into the “Instructions” field > Save.

## Create Your Worker Agents
# Click “Create Agent” again > Name: “ResponseAgent”
# System prompt:
You are a Response Agent.

ORIGINAL REQUEST:
{{input}}

ROUTING DECISION:
{{LatestMessage}}

Your job:
- Provide a clear, user-friendly answer
- Use the ORIGINAL REQUEST

Return final response only.

# # Paste this prompt into the “Instructions” field > Save.

## Connect Your Agents Using Workflow
# Click “Workflow” > Sequential Workflow > Click “Create Flow”
# Assign an agent to the agent nodes by selecting each agent node in the workflow and either selecting the desired agent or creating a new one. 
# Choose the "Masteragent" as node
# use if/else > On if, add the condition: First(Local.LatestMessage).Text = "DataAgent"
# Then, choose the "Dataagent" as node
# On else, choose the "Responseagent" as node

# Save, with a workflow name

